================================================================================
UPSTREAM CREDITS / 上游工作致谢
================================================================================

ChorusKD builds upon and extends the following prior work. These are independent
research contributions by their respective authors and are credited here for
transparency. See the "创新点与出处" section of README.md for a precise statement
of what ChorusKD adds to each.

  - Self-Consistency Improves Chain of Thought Reasoning in Language Models
    Wang et al., ICLR 2023.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.11171
    Origin of the multi-sample consistency voting idea. ChorusKD adapts it to
    black-box teacher outputs with character-level F1 clustering, and adds
    three degenerate-output detectors.

  - Direct Preference Optimization: Your Language Model is Secretly a Reward Model
    Rafailov et al., NeurIPS 2023.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.18290
    Origin of the DPO objective used in the on-policy stage.

  - RRHF: Rank Responses to Align Language Models with Human Feedback
    Yuan et al., NeurIPS 2023.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.05302
    Origin of learning from ranked candidate responses rather than scalar scores.

  - On-Policy Distillation of Language Models (GKD)
    Agarwal et al., ICLR 2024.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.13649
    Source of the self-sampling student-prefix idea. ChorusKD replaces teacher
    distribution scoring (unavailable in black-box) with listwise ranking.

  - MiniLLM: On-Policy Distillation of Large Language Models
    Gu et al., ICLR 2024.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08543
    Background on reverse-KL and on-policy optimization for LLM distillation.

  - Dual-Space Knowledge Distillation for Large Language Models (DSKD)
    Zhang et al., EMNLP 2024.  https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.17328
    Sibling white-box framework; see the companion repository LensKD
    (https://github.com/PassionCR7/LensKD).

